<article class="env-example" id="0EYF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EYF">Example <span data-tag="0EYF">58.31.4</span> <span class="named">(Standard tamely ramified morphism)</span>.</a>  Let $A$ be a Noetherian ring. Let $f \in A$ be a nonzerodivisor such that $A/fA$ is reduced. This implies that $A_\mathfrak p$ is a discrete valuation ring with uniformizer $f$ for any minimal prime $\mathfrak p$ over $f$. Let $e \geq 1$ be an integer which is invertible in $A$. Set </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  C = A[x]/(x^ e - f)  \]
</div>
  <p> Then $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(C) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is a finite locally free morphism which is étale over the spectrum of $A_ f$. The finite étale morphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(C_ f) \longrightarrow \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A_ f)  \]
</div>
  <p> is tamely ramified over $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ in codimension $1$. The tameness follows immediately from the characterization of tamely ramified extensions in More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0EXW" data-tag="0EXW">15.116.7</a>. </p>
</article>